      "id": 1,
      "text": "The George Nakashima Woodworker Complex in Solebury is a National Historic Landmark, honoring a pioneer of modern furniture design.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solebury_Township%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Solebury Township boasts four National Historic Landmarks and six National Historic Districts, with over 400 homes dating back to the 18th and 19th centuries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solebury_Township%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Before European settlement, the area now known as Solebury was inhabited by the Lenape Turtle Tribe, one of three Algonquian groups in the Delaware River valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://soleburyhistory.org/solebury-history/history-of-solebury-township/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1702, English Quakers carved out Solebury Township from Buckingham lands, and by 1703 it already had 24 landowners and 28 farm tracts.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solebury_Township%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Mills powered by local streams produced wood, grain, paper, silk, and limestone products, making Solebury a bustling industrial hub in the 18th and 19th centuries.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solebury_Township%2C_Pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "During the early 1990s, the rock duo Ween recorded their albums *The Pod* and *Pure Guava* in an apartment on Van Sant Road in Solebury.",
